{
  "name": "Turn a CRM export into a filled Excel sales report with DocMint",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "note_overview",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1000,
        -60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 720,
        "height": 1000,
        "content": "## Turn a CRM export into a filled Excel sales report with DocMint\n\n**Who's it for**\nAnyone who exports flat sales rows out of a CRM and has to hand back a formatted `.xlsx` every month — without maintaining a spreadsheet full of formulas and without an Office install anywhere near the workflow.\n\n**How it works**\nThe workflow takes a POST with a `period` and a flat `rows` array, refuses a broken export before a document is rendered, asks DocMint which placeholders the workbook contains, does the arithmetic in a Code node (revenue per row, then a per-region roll-up), fills the `.xlsx` and answers the original request with the file — or with a 422 that says what went wrong.\n\nThe four grey notes on the canvas mark the four stages.\n\n**How to set up**\n1. Add a **DocMint** credential — the free plan is 30 documents a month and needs no card.\n2. Upload your own `.xlsx` to DocMint with placeholders for the fields you want, and put its name into **Set your company and template**. That Set node is the only node you need to edit.\n3. Activate the workflow and POST your export to the production webhook URL.\n\n**Requirements**\n- A DocMint API key from `docmint.app.mintapis.com`.\n- An `.xlsx`, `.docx` or `.pptx` template stored on your DocMint account.\n\n⚠️ **Self-hosted n8n only.** This template uses the `n8n-nodes-docmint` community node, which cannot be installed on n8n Cloud.\n\n**How to customize**\nThe roll-up in **Total the rows and roll up by region** is ordinary JavaScript — group by `rep` or `channel` instead of `region` by changing one key. Set `output` to `both` on the DocMint node to get the `.xlsx` and a PDF in one call. Swap **Return the workbook** for a Gmail, Drive or S3 node to deliver the report instead of returning it.\n\n**Disclosure**\nI build and run DocMint, the service this template calls. This is a self-submission, not a third-party recommendation."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "note_stage1",
      "name": "Sticky Note 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -240,
        120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 680,
        "height": 420,
        "content": "## 1 · Receive and validate the export\n\nPOST a `period`, a `source` and a flat `rows` array. **Set your company and template** is the one node you edit.\n\nAn empty export is refused *before* anything is rendered — a broken payload gets a readable 422, not a workbook full of blanks."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "note_stage2",
      "name": "Sticky Note 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        460,
        20
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 460,
        "height": 420,
        "content": "## 2 · Confirm the template exists\n\n`getFields` reads the `.xlsx` and reports the placeholders it contains.\n\nIt is also the cheapest check that the template is there and the credential works: it renders nothing and costs no credit."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "note_stage3",
      "name": "Sticky Note 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        940,
        20
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 420,
        "height": 420,
        "content": "## 3 · Do the arithmetic, then fill\n\nRevenue per row, then a per-region roll-up with reps, units and prior period, sorted by revenue.\n\nDocMint then expands each array into its own table."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "note_stage4",
      "name": "Sticky Note 4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1380,
        -60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 460,
        "height": 680,
        "content": "## 4 · Always answer the caller\n\nOn success the `.xlsx` goes back on the original request.\n\nIf DocMint could not be reached, the caller gets a 422 with the real reason — never a silently half-filled workbook."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "wh1",
      "name": "Receive the CRM export",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "position": [
        -140,
        300
      ],
      "webhookId": "b2f4c8a1-3d67-4e59-9a12-77c0e5b3d914",
      "parameters": {
        "path": "docmint-sales-report",
        "options": {},
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "responseMode": "responseNode"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "set1",
      "name": "Set your company and template",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "position": [
